The POST /api/sessions/{id}/acceptance-evaluation row in docs/architecture.md (about :414), and the acceptance-evaluation section of docs/features/engram-host-adapter.md, describe the submission's refusals:
- the retryable 502, "the work's naming authority is still being confirmed … nothing was sent; submit the same verdicts again";
- the final 409, "the work's naming authority cannot be confirmed … do not submit again", given at once or after 3 unsettled submissions of one attempt;
- the pre-existing final 409, "source root changed while it was evaluated".
A caller can then tell the retryable answer from the final ones.
